# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  apps/share — Vercel project "apna-ghar-share"  (Root Directory: apps/share)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  TEMPLATE — committed. Copy to .env. `pnpm --filter @ghar/share dev` serves :3002.
#  Vercel bakes env vars in at BUILD time — redeploy after changing one.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ⚠️ NO /api SUFFIX HERE. This app fetches /s/:token, which main.ts explicitly
# excludes from the global `api` prefix. The admin project uses the same
# variable name WITH the suffix — see apps/admin/.env.
#
#   local     http://localhost:3000
#   deployed  https://apna-ghar-api.vercel.app
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Where the "what is Ghar?" link on the landing page points.
#   local     http://localhost:3003
#   deployed  https://apna-ghar-web.vercel.app
WEB_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3003

# The API's SHARE_BASE_URL must point back at THIS app, or the links it mints
# are unopenable. Deployed, that is https://apna-ghar-share.vercel.app
